<name>Navigation</name>
<ttl id="1002Q_S000F_746OU_T00CJ" variety="T00CJ">
<name>HDD Navigation System</name>
<para id="RM0000002RV04DX" category="D" type-id="303F3" name-id="NS5EQ-02" from="200912">
<name>Diagnosis System</name>
<subpara id="RM0000002RV04DX_z0" proc-id="RM0550J___0000IGD00000">
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<step1>
<ptxt>Diagnosis Screen Transitions</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E195385" width="7.106578999in" height="8.799559038in"/>
</figure>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E169547" width="7.106578999in" height="9.803535572in"/>
</figure>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E195366" width="7.106578999in" height="9.803535572in"/>
</figure>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E195367" width="7.106578999in" height="9.803535572in"/>
</figure>
</step1>
<step1>
<ptxt>Starting and Ending Diagnosis</ptxt>
<atten3>
<ptxt>Some items cannot be inspected unless the diagnosis mode is started after turning the ignition ON and confirming that the map screen is displayed.</ptxt>
</atten3>
<atten4>
<ptxt>There are 2 methods for starting diagnosis.</ptxt>
</atten4>
<step2>
<ptxt>Start Method 1</ptxt>
<step3>
<ptxt>Stop the vehicle.</ptxt>
</step3>
<step3>
<ptxt>Turn ACC ON, turn the ignition ON or start the engine.</ptxt>
</step3>
<step3>
<ptxt>While pressing the "INFO/G" switch on the navigation receiver assembly, operate the headlight dimmer switch OFF → TAIL → OFF → TAIL → OFF → TAIL → OFF.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E195383J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<atten4>
<ptxt>If the picture quality adjustment function is set to daytime screen display, cancel the daytime screen display setting before performing the operation.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</step3>
<step3>
<ptxt>When diagnosis starts, the "Service Inspection" screen is displayed.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E150444" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</step3>
</step2>
<step2>
<ptxt>Start Method 2</ptxt>
<step3>
<ptxt>Stop the vehicle.</ptxt>
</step3>
<step3>
<ptxt>Turn ACC ON, turn the ignition ON or start the engine.</ptxt>
</step3>
<step3>
<ptxt>On the map screen, press the "PICTURE/OFF" switch on the navigation receiver assembly to display the picture quality adjustment screen.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E195384J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</step3>
<step3>
<ptxt>On the picture quality adjustment screen, slowly touch the upper left and lower left areas in the order upper left → lower left → upper left → lower left → upper left → lower left.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E150528J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Touch inside the four corners of the picture quality adjustment screen, not the corners of the display.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>If the picture quality adjustment screen is displayed from an NTSC display screen such as the DVD screen, 4 adjustment items, "Tint", "Color", "Contrast" and "Brightness", are displayed. In this case, diagnosis cannot be started even if the above operation is performed.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
</step3>
<step3>
<ptxt>When diagnosis starts, the "Service Inspection" screen is displayed.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E150444" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</step3>
</step2>
<step2>
<ptxt>Cancel Method</ptxt>
<step3>
<ptxt>To cancel, turn the IG OFF.</ptxt>
</step3>
</step2>
</step1>
<step1>
<ptxt>Service Inspection</ptxt>
<atten4>
<ptxt>The service inspection can perform diagnosis, function/information checks and data collection for each component.</ptxt>
</atten4>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E150444" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<step2>
<ptxt>Diagnosis/Diagnosis Information Collection</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E169550" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<table>
<title>Diagnosis/Diagnosis Information Collection Screen Display Contents</title>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.38in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.62in"/>
<colspec colname="COLSPEC0" colwidth="1.13in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Display</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Description</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Reference</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>MM System Diagnosis</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="left">
<ptxt>Displays the names of components connected to the AVC-LAN, collects the current/past DTCs of those components, and displays them as diagnosis results.</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>
<xref label="Seep01" href="RM000000OCQ05TX"/>
</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>HDD Diagnosis</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="left">
<ptxt>Performs diagnosis of the built-in HDD.</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>
<xref label="Seep02" href="RM000000JE903GX_01_0027"/>
</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Diagnosis Information Collection</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="left">
<ptxt>This switch can be pressed but is not used.</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>-</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
<atten4>
<ptxt>Each diagnosis/diagnosis information collection screen is drawn by the navigation receiver assembly.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</step2>
<step2>
<ptxt>Function Check and Adjustment</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E169551" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<table>
<title>Function Inspection/Adjustment Screen Display Contents</title>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.38in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.62in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.13in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Display</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Description</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Reference</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Panel and Steering Switch Check</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Inspects the operating condition of each switch around the display and the steering switches.</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry morerows="6" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>
<xref label="Seep04" href="RM000000JE903GX"/>
</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Touch Switch Check</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Inspects the operating condition of the display touch switches.</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Microphone/Voice Recognition Inspection</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Inspects the microphone connected to the navigation receiver assembly.</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Color Bar Display Check</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Inspects the color display of the display.</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>GPS/Sensor Information</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Displays GPS related information.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Sets the GPS date and time.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Displays information of each sensor in the navigation receiver assembly.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Vehicle Signal Check</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Inspects the condition of vehicle signals input to the display.</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Sound Library Setting</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Displays HDD recording settings and various music server information.</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Hands-free Volume Setting</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Sets the hands-free volume.</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>
<xref label="Seep05" href="RM000001C4801NX"/>
</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Camera Optical Axis Adjustment</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Adjusts the back guide monitor system.</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>
<xref label="Seep06" href="RM0000002O803UX"/>
</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
<atten4>
<ptxt>Each function inspection/adjustment screen is drawn by the navigation receiver assembly.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</step2>
<step2>
<ptxt>Service Information</ptxt>
<atten4>
<ptxt>Service information allows G-BOOK related settings, information checks, and saving and loading of memory.</ptxt>
</atten4>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E122342" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<table>
<title>Service Information Screen Display Contents</title>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.38in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.63in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.12in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Display</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Description</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Reference</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>G Terminal Link Information</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>G-BOOK terminal ID, flag information, etc. are displayed.</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>
<xref label="Seep07" href="RM000001C3T024X"/>
</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>HELPNET/DCM Information</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>HELPNET related ID, contract status, maintenance check date, etc. are displayed.</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>
<xref label="Seep08" href="RM000001C3T024X"/>
</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>HELPNET Report History</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>The history (date and time, status) of HELPNET reports is displayed.</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>
<xref label="Seep09" href="RM000001C3Y021X_01_0003"/>
</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Remote Security Diagnosis</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Remote security inspection results are displayed (not displayed on this model)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>-</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Memory Save/Load</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Saves and loads memory using a tool.</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>-</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
<atten4>
<ptxt>Each service information screen is drawn by the navigation receiver assembly.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</step2>
</step1>
</content5>
</subpara>
</para>
